# Lessons

Automatic on archive, plus "Reflect now" (`POST /v1/chats/:runId/lessons/reflect`): `v1/lessons`.

- A lessons reflection is a thread analysis with `Run.analysisPurpose = 'lessons'`; its optional second-model check is `'lessons_check'` (null or `review` is the user's own "Analyze thread"). Both share the analysis machinery — hidden from every listing, deleted with their source, read through `read_analyzed_thread` — but never replace, hide or are read as the review: `RunDao.listReviewAnalysesOf` is what `findAnalysis`, a start's replace list and `teamLedgerChats` read, and `listAnalysesOf` (every purpose) only the source's delete.
- Stretches (`LessonSegmentService`): archiving a thread (`runs_changed` with `archivedAt`) closes its stretch past `Run.reflectedThroughSeq` and queues it as a `queued` segment when it holds a learning signal (`utils/lesson-signals.fold.ts`, model-free) and reflections are on for the thread — the app's mode (`off` / `auto`), then the team's `lessons` field (library YAML, else the run's copy), then `Project.lessons` (`utils/lessons-mode.ts`); the app's `off` wins. No signal, nothing new or lessons off → nothing. A thread has at most one queued segment; a later close extends it. Nothing else closes a stretch: no outcome, stage, card or quiet-window closers (user decision R1). `POST /v1/lessons/segments/:id/skip` (the archive notice's Skip) moves a `queued` one to `skipped` / `user_skipped` and the watermark past it; 409 `LESSON_SEGMENT_DECIDED` once it started.
- The runner (`LessonAutoRunner`) starts queued segments one at a time, oldest first, an archive's only after `LESSON_ARCHIVE_GRACE_MS` (so Skip can still stop it); a segment holds a `LESSON_SEGMENT_LEASE_MS` lease while it reflects or checks, and a lease that runs out is taken back (the chat cancelled) as a failed attempt. A reflection that settles without filing is a failed attempt too: back to `queued`, and `failed` with its reason (`utils/run-failure.ts`: the run's newest `error` row) after `LESSON_SEGMENT_MAX_ATTEMPTS`. At start it takes back segments whose run ended or is gone. A queued archive segment whose thread has lessons off by then becomes `skipped` / `off`. No spend limit (user decision R2). "Reflect now" and a delete's extraction start their own reflection at once, outside the queue.
- `LessonReflectionService.start` takes the thread's queued segment (else records a new one), reads the items past the watermark up to its snapshot, and starts the chat with `lessonsReflectionGuide` as its `taskInstructions` and a brief naming the stretch, the signals and the lessons kept out of memory in the same team, else project (rejected, undone, dropped by the check). 409 `LESSONS_NOTHING_NEW`, `LESSONS_REFLECTING` (one at a time per thread) and `LESSONS_NOT_REFLECTABLE` (an analysis, builder or project chat). It runs in the source's folder, else its project's, else the userData folder, as `LessonsConfigService.reflectionChoice` says: what a press names, else `LessonsConfig.reflector` (a CLI, profile, model, effort, context window and model parameters pushed by Electron main's `lessons` key), else "same as the thread" — the source's CLI and `configDir`, that CLI's light model (the adapter fact `lightModel`, served on `GET /v1/capabilities`: claude `haiku`, codex `gpt-6-luna`, cursor-agent none → the CLI default) at effort `high` when `EffortsService.accepts` it. Nothing falls back to another CLI or account: a signed-out profile fails like any run.
- A hidden lessons chat has no shell and no write tools: it starts in `ask` (`LESSONS_REFLECTION_APPROVAL`), `runsReadOnly` sets `AgentTurnInput.readOnly` on its turns, and each adapter strips its own CLI's tools — claude `--tools Read,Grep,Glob` with `--strict-mcp-config` (geniro's server only, `claude-in-chrome` switched off), codex `features.shell_tool = false` in the read-only sandbox under `untrusted`, cursor a profile whose `permissions` deny `Shell(*)` and `Write(**)`. `runsReadOnly` also makes the permission gate refuse at once, with no card, every request the rules do not approve; geniro's own tools are approved in every mode. Never `plan`: claude 2.1.316 runs Sonnet under `--permission-mode plan` whatever `--model` says. The card's footer names the model the reflection was billed for (`billedModelOf` over its `turn_complete` rows).
- geniro's MCP server lists a hidden lessons chat only `read_analyzed_thread`, `memory_search`, `memory_read`, `propose_lessons` and `check_lessons` (`mcp/tools/hidden-lessons-gate.ts`): every tool schema rides the prompt prefix each reflection writes to the cache, which measured about 90% of a reflection's cost.
- `propose_lessons` (`mcp/tools/propose-lessons/`, auto-approved by `isHostLessonsCall`) is listed only on a reflection turn (`AnalysisBroker.isReflection`); a hidden lessons chat is refused `report_recommendations`, `mark_recommendations` and `save_team_change` (`canReview`), and `memory_save` / `memory_forget` / `memory_feedback` (`MemoryService.isReflection`). `LessonFilingService` refuses the whole call with every problem named — `TOO_MANY` (over 3), `TOO_LONG`, `EVIDENCE_OUT_OF_SEGMENT`, `QUOTE_NOT_FOUND` (`quoteIn` over the row's strings), `CONTAINS_SECRET` (`redactSecrets`), `UNKNOWN_HANDLE`, `NEAR_DUPLICATE`, `ALREADY_FILED`, `NO_PLACE_FOR_TARGET` (project instructions or knowledge on a thread with no project, member instructions on a thread that is no team run), `UNKNOWN_MEMBER` (not in the run's shared team copy), `UNKNOWN_DOCUMENT` (no active document of the project by that handle) — and otherwise records `lesson_proposals` with the places the thread had (`places`: project id and the team copy's members, `utils/lesson-places.ts`, which the brief also lists) and moves the watermark to the segment's end (never back). Zero lessons → segment `empty`; a card only for "Reflect now".
- Targets (`LessonTarget`): `memory` (scope, type), `project_instructions`, `member_instructions` (member id), `knowledge` (an existing document's handle, or null for a new one). Only a memory lesson with dedup `new` is ever written without the user; every other one stays `proposed` on the card — instructions and knowledge are shared, always-loaded texts, and a `refines` / `broken_again` lesson is the user's to apply.
- Filing at once (user decision R4): each memory-target lesson with dedup `new` goes through `MemoryService.fileLesson` with actor `{kind: 'lesson', runId: <reflection>, …}` — an agent write: near-duplicate check, the review rule (`pending` while `agentWrites` is `pending`), provenance with `Memory.lessonProposalId`, and out of the memory index (`indexable`) until the user approves it or agents' marks promote it (`.claude/rules/daemon-memory.md` → Marks); it is found through `memory_search` at once. The brief lists the memory entries the thread had in front of it (`MemoryService.seenEntries`), and the reflection reports what they did as `propose_lessons.effects`, checked like evidence (inside the stretch, seen by the thread) and recorded as the thread's marks; auto lessons forgotten by marks or expiry join the rejected list (`forgottenLessons`). The proposal becomes `saved` (`resultRef` the handle) or `skipped_duplicate`; a target the thread has no place for stays `proposed` for Save. Then the `lessons` row and one `lesson_outcome` row per lesson (`by: 'auto'`) go into the SOURCE (`LessonRowWriter`, persist-then-emit, an archived source included), and the segment ends `reflected`.
- The check (`LessonCheckService`), only while `LessonsConfig.checker` is set and the reflection found ≥ 1 lesson: the proposals are held `checking` (segment `checking`) and a second hidden chat (`lessons_check`, the checker's CLI, profile, model and effort, `lessonsCheckGuide`) answers through `check_lessons` (`mcp/tools/check-lessons/`, listed by `AnalysisBroker.isLessonCheck`) with one verdict per lesson — refused whole on `UNKNOWN_LESSON`, `MISSING_VERDICT`, `DUPLICATE_VERDICT`, `REWRITE_MISMATCH`, `TOO_LONG`, `CONTAINS_SECRET`. `keep` and `rewrite` (new title and rule, the reflector's evidence) are filed as above; `drop` becomes `dropped_by_check` with its reason, on the card. A check that ends without verdicts is retried up to `LESSON_SEGMENT_MAX_ATTEMPTS`, then its lessons are `check_failed` and wait on the card for Save / Reject. `LessonFilingService.useCheck` is how the check registers, so neither service imports the other's constructor.
- The user's decisions (`LessonProposalService`, all open to a paired device): Save on a `proposed` or `check_failed` lesson writes as the user where its target (as sent, else as proposed) says — a memory entry through `MemoryService.create` (active, indexed); `- <rule>` appended to the project's `lessons` block (created when missing) through `ProjectsService.update` at the revision read, logged with origin `lesson` (the thread as its chat); `- <rule>` appended to the member's instructions in the LIBRARY team through `TeamChangeService.appendMemberLine` (authority `lesson`: hash-guarded against the version read, backed up, logged with source `lesson`; never a project overlay); or a project knowledge document through `KnowledgeService.create`, or a `## <title>` section appended through `edit` at the read rev. "Update rule" (`update-rule`, dedup `refines`) edits the named entry through `MemoryService.edit`; "Move up" (`move-up`, dedup `broken_again`, `moveUpOf`) appends the rule to the project's instructions, else approves the named entry into the index. Reject stores the reason; on a lesson saved to memory Undo forgets the entry (restorable), Edit rewrites it (the entry becomes the user's own), Approve sets it active and approved (indexed) — refused `LESSON_NOT_FILED` for a lesson saved anywhere else. Each writes a `lesson_outcome` row (newest per proposal wins; `resultRef` names where it landed), skipped when the source thread is gone. `GET /v1/lessons/proposals?status=proposed,check_failed` is Settings → Memory's Waiting for review → Lessons list: every waiting lesson, a deleted thread's included (`sourceExists`).
- Spend: a reflection's turns carry `usage_events.purpose = 'lessons'` and a check's `'lessons_check'` (`usageDimensions`, live and in the backfill), summed as `byPurpose` on `GET /v1/stats/usage`; `GET /v1/lessons/spend` (`LessonSpendService`) folds every row of today and this month by step, counts runs with no reported cost as unpriced (never $0) and lists failed segments with their reasons; the card's footer reads `GET /v1/lessons/reflections/:id` (a reflection or its check) over that run's ledger rows. `GET /v1/lessons/estimate` prices the reflection and, with a checker, the check (`LessonEstimateService`: the stretch's payload characters and the guide's over 4, plus `LESSON_READ_OVERHEAD_TOKENS`, read `LESSON_READ_PASSES` times, each pass at the context tier its prompt reaches, plus `LESSON_ANSWER_TOKENS`; no list price → `usd: null`, never 0).
- Delete with "Extract lessons first" (`?extractLessons=true` on the chat and team-run delete routes): the routes ask `ExtractLessonsOnDeleteRegistry` (in `AgentsModule`, filled by `LessonPendingDeleteService`, so neither route's module imports this one). It sets `Run.pendingDeleteAt`, archives, starts the reflection with closer `delete`, and deletes through `ChatService.delete` / `TeamExecutorService.deleteRun` once the stretch has ended (`reflected`, `empty`, `failed` or `skipped`, heard on `lessons_changed`), after `LESSON_PENDING_DELETE_MAX_MS`, or at the next start. Nothing to reflect on → the route deletes at once. Every listing (`RunDao.listPage`, `listThreads`, `countByShelf`) and the chat search (`ChatSearchIndexDao.match` / `run`) leave a pending run out. A reflection already working on the thread is waited for instead of starting a second; any other failure clears `pendingDeleteAt` and the route deletes at once.
